WEBVTT

00:00:07.916 --> 00:00:09.500
[stomping, rumbling]

00:00:11.041 --> 00:00:12.375
[trumpeting]

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:22.458
-[rumbling]
-[elephants trumpeting]

00:00:22.541 --> 00:00:25.791
[Bonnie]
So, saw you on TV.
You okay?

00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:27.375
Everything's fine, Mom.

00:00:27.458 --> 00:00:30.083
[Stu]
Uh-oh. Everyone knows
"fine" is a cry for help.

00:00:30.166 --> 00:00:31.500
You know who else
cried for help?

00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:32.750
That dik-dik
stuck in that tuba.

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:35.708
Oh, him and the dik-dik. What
does your fox partner say?

00:00:35.791 --> 00:00:39.708
[Judy]
Well, Nick's
not really a talker.

00:00:40.291 --> 00:00:42.875
[Bonnie]
Well, you two
are very different.

00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:45.208
Small-town hero
raised on a farm.

00:00:45.291 --> 00:00:47.083
Big-city crook
raised on the streets.

00:00:47.166 --> 00:00:48.166
I pray every day

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.000
that you'll come back home
and make babies.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.125
[Bonnie]
Mom!

00:00:51.208 --> 00:00:52.583
Just remember the first rule
of partnerships.

00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:54.583
You can be right
or you can be happy.

00:00:54.666 --> 00:00:55.500
That's true.

00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:57.250
[Stu]
There's nothing wrong
with dying a little inside

00:00:57.333 --> 00:00:58.541
so you can meet in the middle.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:00:59.583
Honey, you're pushing me out.

00:00:59.666 --> 00:01:00.791
I wanna make sure
I can be seen.

00:01:00.875 --> 00:01:01.875
[Bonnie]
Well, if she
could see both of us.

00:01:01.958 --> 00:01:03.541
-Gotta go. Work to do.
-
[Bonnie]
Bye, bun-bun.

00:01:03.625 --> 00:01:04.916
[Stu]
Everything's gonna be fine.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.500
-You two just need a new case.
-Got it. Love you.

00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:08.083
Maybe try to find
that dik-dik.

00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:09.000
Bye.

00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:10.458
[sighs]

00:01:17.791 --> 00:01:18.833
[sighs]

00:01:18.916 --> 00:01:21.750
-[♪ vocalizing theme music]
-[laughing]

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:23.750
[audience]
Squeal of Fortune!

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:26.666
Tomorrow's weather is,
again, everything.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:27.791
[Purrrnacleo]
...to announce that

00:01:27.875 --> 00:01:30.083
the long-awaited Tundratown expansion
will be starting soon.

00:01:30.166 --> 00:01:31.208
CARROTS for ONE

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.166
Residents continue
to raise concerns

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.041
about the future
of their neighborhood.

00:01:35.125 --> 00:01:38.916
[Howlett]
But tonight
we put our differences aside

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.833
and celebrate
at the Zootennial gala,

00:01:40.916 --> 00:01:43.375
where the Lynxley Journal
will be on display

00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:45.708
for the first time
in a century,

00:01:45.791 --> 00:01:48.291
following an infamous
reptile attack.

00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:50.208
The Lynxley Journal,

00:01:50.291 --> 00:01:52.291
containing the patented
weather wall plans,

00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:54.958
was originally written by
Ebenezer Lynxley,

00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:55.958
bringing the whole...

00:02:10.666 --> 00:02:12.333
Same catering company.

00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:15.791
Mmm.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:26.750
The Lynxley journal.

00:02:34.208 --> 00:02:35.875
SCALES AND TALES OF THE WEIRD
WITH NIBBLES MAPLESTICK

00:02:35.958 --> 00:02:38.333
Truth bomb! The 100th anniversary
of the weather walls

00:02:38.416 --> 00:02:40.833
is also the 100th anniversary

00:02:40.916 --> 00:02:43.333
of Zootropolis's
only snake attack.

00:02:43.916 --> 00:02:45.958
The victim? A tortoise.

00:02:46.041 --> 00:02:48.916
The Lynxley family maid

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.750
who was fanged while stopping
a venomous snake

00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:54.250
from stealing
the Lynxley Journal.

00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:56.958
No one has seen a snake
in Zootropolis since.

00:02:57.041 --> 00:03:00.541
But I'm convinced
one will return.

00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:02.250
My only question is,

00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:07.458
is he gonna be wearing
half-a-pants or one long sock?

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:15.125
-[villain groans]
-You say, "Justice is dead."

00:03:15.208 --> 00:03:17.333
I say, "Neigh!"

00:03:17.875 --> 00:03:18.708
Ha-cha!

00:03:19.291 --> 00:03:21.458
[Winddancer shouting]

00:03:21.541 --> 00:03:22.375
[villain groaning]

00:03:22.458 --> 00:03:24.083
Well, well,
you miss me already, huh?

00:03:24.166 --> 00:03:25.375
[Judy]
The stolen van
with the snake skin

00:03:25.458 --> 00:03:26.791
is from the same
catering company

00:03:26.875 --> 00:03:28.250
-that's working the gala.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:30.666
This is you studying
your partner book?

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.250
Listen to me. Venomous snakes

00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:34.333
tried to steal
the Lynxleys's journal before.

00:03:34.416 --> 00:03:36.208
What if they're back in town
to steal it again?

00:03:36.291 --> 00:03:37.750
-No snake has set foot...
-[knocking]

00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:40.458
...in Zootropolis in forever,
okay?

00:03:40.541 --> 00:03:42.125
Even if they had feet.
[chuckles]

00:03:42.208 --> 00:03:43.500
Look, we're already
in the hot seat, Carrots,

00:03:43.583 --> 00:03:45.083
and pizza's here. Gotta go--

00:03:45.166 --> 00:03:46.208
If there's a fanging
at the gala

00:03:46.291 --> 00:03:47.416
and we do nothing to stop it,

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.333
then we are not
doing our jobs...

00:03:49.416 --> 00:03:52.208
Yikes. No wonder
you never invite me over.

00:03:52.291 --> 00:03:53.791
Foxes are solitary.

00:03:53.875 --> 00:03:56.000
And, look, we go
and you're wrong,

00:03:56.083 --> 00:03:57.125
Chief Beef will split us up.

00:03:57.208 --> 00:03:58.250
And if we don't get a win soon

00:03:58.333 --> 00:03:59.625
and prove
we're great partners,

00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:01.625
the chief will
split us up anyway.

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.166
Check the perimeter.
Snoop a little.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.000
We find nothing, we bail.

00:04:05.083 --> 00:04:06.208
But if I'm right,

00:04:06.291 --> 00:04:07.333
no one will question

00:04:07.416 --> 00:04:09.458
whether you and I
belong together again.

00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:11.375
We need this.

00:04:12.791 --> 00:04:13.833
Fine.

00:04:13.916 --> 00:04:16.375
But we'll still have
to get through security,

00:04:16.458 --> 00:04:17.916
and in fancy town,
a fox and a bunny

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.291
won't exactly blend in. Oof!

00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:22.375
[Judy] That's why
we'll be undercover!

00:04:22.458 --> 00:04:23.500
[engine revving]

00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:25.791
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Shakira "Zoo"]

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.708
See you're still
in the driver's seat. Whoa!

00:04:28.791 --> 00:04:31.000
[Gazelle singing]
♪
Come on, get on up
♪

00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:33.041
♪
We're wild
And we can't be tamed
♪

00:04:33.125 --> 00:04:36.125
♪
And we're turning the floor
Into a zoo-ooh-ooh
♪

00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:37.041
Here we go!

00:04:37.125 --> 00:04:38.125
Here we go! Let's go!

00:04:39.625 --> 00:04:41.500
Zootropolis, let me hear ya!

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:47.666
♪
We live in a crazy world
Caught up in a rat race
♪

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:51.125
♪
Concrete jungle life
Is sometimes a mad place
♪

00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:54.625
♪
It's you and me together
At the end of a wild day
♪

00:04:54.708 --> 00:04:58.375
♪
Don't keep it all bottled up
And release your energy
♪

00:05:00.041 --> 00:05:03.875
♪
Only reason we are here
Is to celebrate
♪

00:05:03.958 --> 00:05:07.541
♪
In a place where anyone
Can be anything
♪

00:05:07.625 --> 00:05:11.000
♪
Hold on to this moment
Don't let it fade away
♪

00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:13.458
♪
Baby
Keep the music playin'
♪

00:05:13.541 --> 00:05:15.375
♪
Come on, get on up
♪

00:05:15.458 --> 00:05:17.750
♪
We're wild
And we can't be tamed
♪

00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:20.958
♪
And we're turnin' the floor
Into a zoo-ooh-ooh
♪

00:05:21.041 --> 00:05:22.916
♪
Come on, keep it up
♪

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.208
♪
It's fun if
You're down to play
♪

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:28.125
♪
And we're turnin' the floor
Into a zoo-ooh-ooh
♪

00:05:29.166 --> 00:05:30.625
[Clawhauser grunts]

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.916
Ah, cats and lights.
I know better.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.791
♪
A zoo-ooh-ooh
♪

00:05:35.875 --> 00:05:37.583
♪
Come on, get on up
♪

00:05:37.666 --> 00:05:40.083
♪
We're wild
And we can't be tamed
♪

00:05:40.166 --> 00:05:43.250
♪
And we're turnin' the floor
Into a zoo-ooh-ooh
♪

00:05:43.333 --> 00:05:45.041
Mayor Winddancer
has arrived...

00:05:45.125 --> 00:05:45.958
Ha-cha!

00:05:46.041 --> 00:05:48.583
...star of the revenge
trilogy,
The Neigh-sayer
.

00:05:48.666 --> 00:05:50.166
No pictures, please.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.208
[laughs] Come on. It's me.

00:05:52.291 --> 00:05:54.666
And that, and that one,
and then this one.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.791
Mr. Lynxley,
when will you begin

00:05:56.875 --> 00:05:58.125
-the Tundratown expansion?
-Come on, Dad.

00:05:58.208 --> 00:06:00.666
Have a wonderful time
at the party.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.291
♪
It's fun if
You're down to play
♪

00:06:02.375 --> 00:06:05.625
♪
And we're turning the floor
Into a zoo-ooh-ooh
♪

00:06:05.708 --> 00:06:07.375
[crowd cheering]

00:06:11.583 --> 00:06:13.708
-[fireworks banging]
-[crowd cheering]

00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:17.041
[yelps]

00:06:17.125 --> 00:06:18.125
D'oh.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.416
[Judy] No snow.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:24.500
Hmm.

00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:25.875
This one's warmer.

00:06:26.375 --> 00:06:29.375
A reptile in Tundratown might
need that to survive the cold.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.250
-[Nick] Oh, my God. A viper!
-[gasps]

00:06:33.791 --> 00:06:36.250
[German accent]
A "vindow viper."
Ja
.

00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:37.541
[chuckles, winces]

00:06:39.125 --> 00:06:40.041
[gasps]

00:06:40.958 --> 00:06:42.000
Back door ajar.

00:06:42.583 --> 00:06:44.083
[Nick] Anyone could have
left it like that.

00:06:44.166 --> 00:06:45.583
And you said,
"Snoop a little,"

00:06:45.666 --> 00:06:47.125
not break and enter-- Oh, God!

00:06:48.291 --> 00:06:49.958
Oh, we were always
going inside. Got it.

00:06:50.041 --> 00:06:51.583
Same page means your page.

00:06:51.666 --> 00:06:53.208
It's called a hustle,
sweetheart.

00:06:53.291 --> 00:06:54.833
You change out here.
I get the van.

